  "title": "The trisum law: the knot's not-all-equal rule one level up",
  "subject": "The amplitude of three non-colourable cubic pieces glued along a square",
  "conclusion": "A trisum of three non-colourable cubic pieces along a square has amplitude rho1 rho2 rho3 - alpha1 alpha2 alpha3 - beta1 beta2 beta3, where (alpha, beta) splits a piece's colourings by the square point its far line leans to. The knot's not-all-equal rule reappears one level up on the pieces' leanings, and pieces glued further down act only as weights on these two numbers.",
